    "recommendations": "Ensuring the single access point and extended driveway remain clear of obstructions at all times could significantly improve emergency vehicle entry and exit, particularly given the presence of multiple structures on the property. Marking or maintaining visible address identification near the street frontage may assist responding units in locating the property quickly. Where dense vegetation borders the driveway or approaches to either structure, periodic management of that growth could improve visibility and maneuvering room for larger emergency vehicles. Identifying and communicating any secondary access pathway to the rear of the property with local emergency services may support more effective staging and operational flexibility during a response."
